solid 52.5 mg (0.099 mmol, 99%). 1H‐NMR (500 MHz, CD2Cl2) δ = 7.87‐7.83
(m, 2H), 7.77‐7.73 (m,2H), 7.62 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 7.44 (d, J = 7.7 Hz,
1H), 7.18 (d, J =8.1 Hz, 1H), 7.09 (ddd, J = 8.0, 7.1, 1.0 Hz, 1H), 7.05
(ddd, J =7.4, 7.4, 0.9 Hz, 1H), 6.76 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 5.25 (d, J =
17.1 Hz, 1H), 5.20 (d, J = 17.1 Hz, 1H), 4.69‐4.58 (m, 1H), 3.50 (dd, J =
14.1, 11.7 Hz, 1H), 2.98 (dd, J =14.6, 5.5 Hz, 1H), 2.91‐2.79 (m, 3H),
2.12‐2.05 (m, 1H) ppm. 13C‐NMR (125 MHz, CD2Cl2) δ = 168.7, 138.4, 138.1,
137.3, 134.5, 134.3, 132.5, 128.5, 127.5,123.3, 121.5, 119.5, 118.2,
109.3, 108.8, 92.7, 48.4, 46.3, 27.1, 25.1, 22.4 ppm. MS (EI) m/z (%):
532 (54), 385 (100), 359 (10), 258 (12), 217 (29), 168 (35). HRMS (ESI+)
m/z calculated for C27H21N2O2INa (M+Na+) 555.053992, found 555.054480.
Mp: 256‐257 °C (CH2Cl2). [α]D25: ‐2.80 °, c = 0.50 (CH2Cl2, er =
93.5:6.5). The enantiomeric ratio was determined by HPLC analysis using
Daicel Chiralpak AD‐3 column: n‐heptane:i‐PrOH = 80:20, flow rate 1.0
mL/min, λ = 220 nm: τ1 = 9.69 min, τ2 =14.32 min. (The sample was
dissolved in CH2Cl2).
