$DATUM Tetrahydrocarbazoles General procedure: A reaction vial was charged with
catalyst 5f (3.33 mg, 0.005 mmol), Amberlite® CG50 (200 mg), the
corresponding hydrazone 1a‐1q (0.100 mmol) and molecular sieves 4Å (50
mg).Under an atmosphere of argon, benzene (1.0 mL) was added and the
resulting mixture was stirred in the sealed vial at 30 °C until complete
conversion was indicated by TLC. The crude reaction mixture was directly
submitted to column chromatography on SiO2. The racemates were prepared
by heating a 1:1 mixture of the corresponding hydrazone and diphenyl
phosphate to 80 °C in toluene for 1 h. The crude reaction mixture was
directly submitted to column chromatography on SiO2.
(S)‐9‐Benzyl‐3‐phenyl‐2,3,4,9‐tetrahydro‐1H‐carbazole (2a) Purification:
Hexane:EtOAc (9:1). Colorless solid 31.8 mg (0.094 mmol, 94%). 1H‐NMR
(500 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 7.43 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H), 7.29‐7.25 (m,4H),
7.22‐7.14 (m, 5H), 7.08‐7.04 (m, 1H), 7.04‐7.01 (m, 1H), 6.95 (d, J= 7.1
Hz, 2H), 5.23 (d, J = 16.9 Hz, 1H), 5.19 (d, J = 16.9 Hz, 1H), 3.09‐3.05
(m, 1H), 3.04‐2.98 (m, 1H), 2.84‐2.79 (m, 1H), 2.73‐2.68 (m, 2H),
2.18‐2.12 (m, 1H), 2.08‐1.98 (m, 1H) ppm. 13C‐NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ =
146.8, 138.3, 137.0, 135.3, 128.9, 128.6, 127.4, 127.3, 127.2,126.4,
126.3, 121.1, 119.2, 117.9, 109.9, 109.2, 46.5, 41.1, 30.5, 29.5, 22.5
ppm. MS (EI) m/z (%): 337 (70), 233 (100), 218 (14), 142 (5), 115 (7), 91
(34). HRMS (EI) m/z calculated for C25H23N 337.183049, found 337.183072.
The enantiomeric ratio was determined by reversed phase HPLC analysis
using Daicel Chiralcel OJ‐RH column: MeCN:H2O = 90:10, flow rate 1.0
mL/min, λ = 220 nm: τ1 = 5.10 min, τ2 = 7.87 min.
