$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Tetrahydrocarbazoles General procedure: A
reaction vial was charged with catalyst 5f (3.33 mg, 0.005 mmol),
Amberlite® CG50 (200 mg), the corresponding hydrazone 1a‐1q (0.100 mmol)
and molecular sieves 4Å (50 mg).Under an atmosphere of argon, benzene
(1.0 mL) was added and the resulting mixture was stirred in the sealed
vial at 30 °C until complete conversion was indicated by TLC. The crude
reaction mixture was directly submitted to column chromatography on SiO2.
The racemates were prepared by heating a 1:1 mixture of the corresponding
hydrazone and diphenyl phosphate to 80 °C in toluene for 1 h. The crude
reaction mixture was directly submitted to column chromatography on SiO2.
(S)‐9‐Benzyl‐3‐phenyl‐2,3,4,9‐tetrahydro‐1H‐carbazole (2a) Purification:
Hexane:EtOAc (9:1).
(S)‐9‐(4‐Iodobenzyl)‐5,7‐dimethyl‐3‐phenyl‐2,3,4,9‐tetrahydro‐1H‐carbazole
(2f) Purification: Hexane:EtOAc (9:1). Colorless solid 44.1 mg (0.090
mmol, 90%). 1H‐NMR (400 MHz, CD2Cl2) δ = 7.51‐7.48 (m, 2H), 7.22 (d, J =
1.4 Hz, 2H), 7.14‐7.11 (m, 1H), 6.69 (s, 1H), 6.65‐6.62 (m, 2H), 6.52(s,
1H), 5.07 (d, J = 17.1 Hz, 1H), 5.02 (d, J = 17.1 Hz, 1H), 3.32‐3.24 (m,
1H), 3.00‐2.90 (m, 2H), 2.63‐2.59 (m, 2H), 2.48 (s, 3H),2.24 (s, 3H),
2.09‐2.02 (m, 1H), 2.00‐1.92 (m, 1H) ppm. 13C‐NMR (100 MHz, CD2Cl2) δ =
147.4, 138.9, 138.1, 137.6, 134.1, 131.0, 130.3, 128.8, 128.6,127.5,
126.5, 124.5, 122.6, 110.7, 107.1, 92.6, 46.1, 32.5, 22.7, 21.7, 20.0
ppm. MS (EI) m/z (%): 460 (47), 243 (100), 217 (13), 187 (5). HRMS (ESI+)
m/z calculated for C27H26NINa (M+Na+) 514.100212, found 514.100342. The
enantiomeric ratio was determined by reversed phase HPLC analysis using
Daicel Chiralcel OJ‐RH column: MeCN:H2O = 90:10, flow rate 1.0 mL/min, λ
= 220 nm: τ1 = 14.84 min, τ2 = 19.55 min.
