$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Chloroaluminate Ionic Liquid17 Freshly
sublimed AlCl3 (134 g, 1 mol) was added to n-BuPyCl (50 g, 0.5 mol) at
r.t. under N2 to give the chloroaluminate ionic liquid. Cyclization of
Arylhydrazones of Ketones 1-11 Using Ionic Liquid;
2-Phenyl-3-methylindole (3); Typical Procedure A mixture of
phenylhydrazine (0.9 g, 8.3 mmol) and propiophenone (1.1 g, 8.3 mmol) was
added dropwise to ionic liquid (1.5 mL, 6.5 mmol), at 180-185 °C for 3 h
under efficient stirring under N2. After the reaction was complete
(monitored by TLC), it was quenched with H2O/concd HCl, extracted with
Et2O, and the Et2O solution was passed through anhyd Na2SO4. The Et2O was
removed to obtain the desired product, which was purified either by
recrystallization (EtOH) or by silica gel column chromatography using
petroleum ether (bp 60-80 °C)/EtOAc (99:1) mixture as the eluent.
2,3,5-Trimethylindole (9) Yield: 1.2 g (90%). Mp found: 118-120 °C;
reported: 121 °C. IR (KBr): ν = 3400 cm-1 (NH). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3):
δ = 2.2 (s, 3 H, CH3), 2.34 (s, 3 H, CH3), 2.44 (s, 3 H, CH3), 6.92-7.57
(m, 4 H, 3 Harom and NH). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 8.36, 11.5,
21.44, 106.64, 109.59, 117.71, 122.28, 128.1, 129.67, 130.7, 133.48.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Chloroaluminate ionic liquid for Fischer indole synthesis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Rebeiro, Geeta L.; Khadilkar, Bhushan M.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2001), (3), 370-372

