$DATUM Step 2. 5,10-Dihydro-2-methoxyindeno[1,2-b]indole (4a) A mixture of
5-methoxy-1-indanone (4-phenyl)-hydrazone (from previous step) (1.2 g,
4.8 mmol) and ZnCl2 (1.5 g, 11 mmol) in AcOH (15 mL) was heated to 120°C
for 2 h. The mixture was then poured into water, extracted with ethyl
acetate. The organic phase was dried with MgSO4 and concentrated. The
product was purified by flash chromatography (ethyl acetate/petroleum,
1/12) to give a white solid. Yield: 0.95 g, (89.9%).
5,10-Dihydro-2-methoxyindeno[1,2-b]indole (4a). Yield 0.95 g, (89.9%).
M.p.: 190-5°C. 1HNMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 4.35 (s, 2H, CH2), 4.48 (s, 3H,
OCH3), 6.94 (dd, 1H, J = 2, 6.8 Hz, ArH), 7.16 (dd, 3H, J = 2.8, 4.8 Hz,
ArH), 7.34 (d, 1H, J = 2.8 Hz, ArH), 7.38 (m, 1H, ArH), 7.53 (dd, 1H, J =
2.8, 4.8 Hz, ArH). MS (EI): m/e (%) 235 (100 M+), 220 (100), 191 (60).
