$DATUM Compound 4 (R = H). (1) A dry HCl flow was passed through a solution of
0.3 g of compound 2 (R = H) in 7 mL of ethyl alcohol and 3 mL of DMF for
6 h at 90°C. The reaction mixture was cooled and poured into water with
ice, and then an aqueous solution of NaOH was added with stirring to pH
5.5-6. The precipitate was filtered off, washed with water, and dried in
air. Yield, 0.26 g (89%). mp 158-160 (DMF-H2O). IR (KBr, ν, cm-1): 772 ,
792 (1,2-disubstituted benzene ring); 840, 896 (1,2,4-trisubstituted
benzene ring); 2936 (NH); (3426 (OH), 960 (OH), 1652 (C═O) (in COOH));
(1720 (C═O), 1232 (C-O-C) (in COOC2H5)). UV (λmax, nm (logε)): 211.06
(3.68), 212.13 (3.68), 214.32 (3.69), 215.42 (3.69), 217.30 (3.69),
268.67 (3.61), 275.18 (3.61), 276.39 (3.61), 280.72 (3.62), 283.29
(3.62), 342.23 (3.40), 366.30 (3.37). 1H NMR (250 MHz, δ, ppm): 1.08 (m,
3H, CH3CH2) , 2.68 (s, 3H, CH3), 4.38 (q, 2H, CH3CH2) , 7.67 (m, 1H,
7-H), 7.84 (m, 1H, 6-H), 8.28 (d, 1H, 5-H), 8.41 (s, 1H, OH), 8.49 (d,
2H, 10,11-H), 8.53 (s, 1H, 3-H), 8.61 (d, 1H, 8-H), 10.23 (s, 1H, NH),
11.64 (s, 1H, COOH). For C22H18N2O4 anal. calcd. (%): C, 70.57; H, 4.84;
N, 7.48. Found (%): C, 70.43; H, 5.02; N, 7.13.
