$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM p-Nitroacetophenone 2-(p-Nitrophenyl)indol-6-ylhydrazone (4). Conc. H2SO4
(3 ml) was added to a solution of dihydrazone 1 (1.3 g, 3 mmol) in
absolute ethanol (15 ml) and refluxed for 3 h. The product was cooled,
poured into crushed ice (150 g) and then filtered, washed with water to
neutral reaction and dried. Yield of product 4. Purification was carried
out on a silica gel column with benzene-ether (3:1) as eluent. 1.03 g
(83%). Rf 0.54 (benzene-acetone, 3:1). Mp 210-212 °C. IR spectrum, ν,
cm-1: 3355, 3335 (NH), 1630 (>C=N); 1560, 1345 (NO2). 1H NMR spectrum, δ,
ppm (J, Hz): 9.61 (1H, s, NH); 9.21 (1H, s, NH); 8.29, 8.20, 7.73 (8H,
three d, two AB systems, J = 9.2 and J = 8.8, Ar); 8.22 (1H, d, J = 1.8,
H-7); 8.12 (1H, d, J = 2.2, H-3); 7.67 (1H, d, J = 8.1, H-4); 7.57 (1H,
dd, J = 1.8 and J = 8.1, H-5); 2.43 (3H, s, CH3). Found: m/z 415.1283
[M]+. C22H17N5O4. Calculated: M 415.4058.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, alternative reaction conditions shown, Fischer reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Indole derivatives. Some aspects of the E. Fischer reaction
