$DATUM Compound 4 (R = Br). Dry HCl was passed through a solution of 0.3 g of
compound 2 (R = Br) in 7 mL of ethyl alcohol and 3 mL of DMF at 90°C for
6 h. After cooling, the mixture was poured into water with ice and
alkalized with an aqueous NaOH solution to pH 5.5-6. The precipitate was
filtered off, washed with water, and dried in air. Yield, 0.24 g (83%).
mp 228-230°C with decomposition (DMF-H2O). IR (KBr, ν, cm-1): 828, 868
(1,2,4-trisubstituted benzene ring); (3435 (OH), 960 (OH), 1660 (C═O) (in
COOH)), (1708 (C═O), 1232 (C-O-C) (in COOC2H5)); 656 (C-Br). UV (λmax, nm
(logε)): 259.43 (2.83), 340.76 (2.56), 381.19 (2.33), 530.05 (1.47),
551.08 (1.47), 563.51 (1.47). 1H NMR (250 MHz, δ, ppm): 1.32 (m, 3H,
CH3CH2), 2.53 (s, 3H, CH3), 4.29 (q, 2H, CH3CH2), 7.55 (d, 1H, 7-H), 7.97
(d, 1H, 6-H), 8.08 (s, 1H, 9-H), 8.12 (s, 1H, 5-H), 8.29 (d, 2H,
10,11-H), 8.51 (s, 1H, 3-H), 8.97 (d, 1H, 8-H), 10.25 (s, 1H, NH). For
C22H17BrN2O4 anal. calcd. (%): C, 58.29; H, 3.78; N, 6.18. Found (%): C,
58.61; H, 3.63; N, 5.92.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
