$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Potassium 3-(4-carboxybutyl)-2,3-dimethylindolenine-5-sulfonate (16b). A
mixture of 4-hydrazinobenzenesulfonic acid (15b) (1.8 g, 9.7 mmol),
6-methyl-7-oxooctanoic acid (8) (2.0 g, 11.6 mmol) and glacial AcOH (15
mL) was refluxed with stirring for 8 h. Then another portion of AcOH (15
mL) was added and the mixture was treated with activated charcoal. The
solvent was removed and the residue was dissolved in MeOH (10 mL). A
solution of KOH (600 mg, 10.6 mmol) in MeOH (7 mL), PriOH (15 mL) and
Et2O (2 mL) was added dropwise. The precipitate that formed was filtered
off and dried in a vacuum desiccator over P2O5. The yield of potassium
salt 16b was 3.5 g (83%), light beige crystals. UV (MeOH), λmax/nm: 258;
m.p. 198—200 °C. Found: m/z 327.2 [M -K]+. C15H19NO5S. Calculated: M =
325.38. 1H NMR (D2O), δ: 0.45—0.70 (m, 2 H, CH2CH2CH2CH2COOH); 1.31 (s, 3
H, H3C(3)); 1.36 (m, 2 H, CH2CH2CH2CH2COOH); 1.88—2.14 (m, 4 H,
CH2CH2CH2CH2COOH); 7.53 (d, 1 H, Ar, J = 9 Hz); 7.80 (m, 2 H, Ar).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Fischer synthesis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of carboxyalkylindolenines from 6-methyl-7-oxooctanoic acid
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kuznetsova, V. E.; Chudinov, A. V.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Russian Chemical Bulletin (2008), 57(3), 608-611

