$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2-Ethoxycarbonyl-5-nitroindole (4); Typical
Procedure (or Fischer Indole Syntheses: Ethyl
2-(4-nitrophenylhydrazono)-propanoate (3,4-nitrophenylhydrazone of ethyl
pyruvate; 1.5 g, ∼7 mmol) is added to a stirred suspension of PPA (6 g)
in xylene (15 ml) at 80 °C. The mixture is heated at 110°C for 1 h, then
washed with water (3 × 15 ml), dried with magnesium sulfate, and
evaporated to dryness in vacuo. The product is recrystallized from
diisopropyl ether. Compound No. 4.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
